s is a geometric series with the first term \\( a = 100 \\times (1 + 0.10/12)^{24} \\) and common ratio \\( r = (1 + 0.10/12) \\).\n\nThe sum of the series is:\n\\[ S = 100 \\times \\frac{(1 + 0.10/12)^{24} \\times ((1 + 0.10/12) - 1)}{(1 + 0.10/12) - 1} \\]\n\\[ S = 100 \\times \\frac{(1 + 0.10/12)^{24} \\times 0.10/12}{0.10/12} \\]\n\\[ S = 100 \\times (1 + 0.10/12)^{24} \\]\n\\[ S \\approx 100 \\times 1.26824 = 126.824 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total amount\n\nThe total amount after two years is the sum of the initial investment with interest, plus the interest earned on the monthly contributions:\n\\[ 1210 + 126.824 = 1336.824 \\]\n\nTherefore, Joseph will have approximately $1336.82 in the fund after two years.",
